 "description": "Check that payment allocations are arithmetically consistent with the invoices and payments they refer to. An over-allocated invoice and an over-allocated payment are reported separately because they are different events: money applied beyond what was owed, and money applied that was never received. Also reports an unallocated remainder, an allocation to a cancelled invoice, and a cross-currency allocation, which converts at a rate the data does not state. Pay 180000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "allocations": {
    "example": [
     {
      "amount": "500.01",
      "invoice": "INV-1",
      "payment": "PAY-1"
     },
     {
      "amount": "50.00",
      "invoice": "INV-2",
      "payment": "PAY-1"
     },
     {
      "amount": "100.00",
